    "analysis": {
      "interpretation": "Across three seeds per model on the bundled digits dataset, the selected candidate achieved 87.78% accuracy under synthetic Gaussian noise versus 37.69% for the baseline, a gain of 50.09 percentage points. Noise macro-F1 increased from 0.39089 to 0.87712. Clean accuracy decreased from 97.50% to 95.19%, a loss of 2.31 percentage points; clean macro-F1 decreased from 0.97498 to 0.95166. These measurements support a robustness–clean-performance tradeoff in this tested setting. Baseline and ablation_no_augmentation are aliases for one control, not independent evidence.",
      "limitations": [
        "Evidence is limited to the bundled digits benchmark and the tested synthetic Gaussian corruption; the dataset itself is real.",
        "Three seeds share one held-out sample set. Seed standard deviations describe seed variability, not confidence intervals or statistical significance.",
        "Augmentation doubles training examples, so an equal-compute advantage is not established.",
        "Summary measurements do not establish manuscript quality, citation accuracy, source coverage, novelty, or venue compliance. Review assertions about artifact verification were not independently verified in this revision."
      ],
      "follow_up": [
        "Revise the report to present the 50.09-percentage-point noise-accuracy gain alongside the 2.31-percentage-point clean-accuracy loss.",
